      "nonempty_text": true,
      "repetition_onset": null,
      "substantive_text": "To find out how many pieces of pizza Albert eats in one day, we need to calculate the number of large pizzas he buys by the number of slices per large pizza and then add the number of small from the small pizzas.\n2 large pizzas * 16 slices per large pizza = 32 slices\n2 small pizzas * 8 slices per small pizza = 16 slices\n3. together, Albert eats 32 + 16 = 48 slices of pizza in one day.\nSo, Albert eats 48 pieces of pizza in one day.",
      "teacher_answer": "48",
      "teacher_answer_match": true,
      "teacher_text": "To find out how many pieces of pizza Albert eats in one day, we need to multiply the number of large pizzas he buys by the number of slices per large pizza and then add the number of slices from the small pizzas.\n2 large pizzas * 16 slices per large pizza = 32 slices\n2 small pizzas * 8 slices per small pizza = 16 slices\nAdding these together, Albert eats 32 + 16 = 48 slices of pizza in one day.\nSo, Albert eats 48 pieces of pizza in one day.<|end_turn|>",
      "teacher_valid_answer_tokens": 111,
      "text": "To find out how many pieces of pizza Albert eats in one day, we need to calculate the number of large pizzas he buys by the number of slices per large pizza and then add the number of small from the small pizzas.\n2 large pizzas * 16 slices per large pizza = 32 slices\n2 small pizzas * 8 slices per small pizza = 16 slices\n3. together, Albert eats 32 + 16 = 48 slices of pizza in one day.\nSo, Albert eats 48 pieces of pizza in one day.<|end_turn|>"
